# Redirects for statically served routes.
#
# Like _headers, this file lives in the project root because
# @sveltejs/adapter-cloudflare requires it there and copies it into the build.
# Cloudflare Pages applies these at its asset handler, before a prerendered
# page is served, so they reach routes the Worker never sees.
#
# These four service pages were retired when the company moved from excavation
# and drainage work to land management. Without a redirect each becomes a 404,
# throwing away any link equity and dropping anyone who arrives from an old
# search result or a saved link.
#
# Small excavation is the closest survivor of the retired set, so it points at
# land clearing. The other three have no equivalent service, and sending them to
# a specific page we do not offer would be worse than honest: they land on the
# services listing, which shows what the company does now.
#
# A test in src/lib/config/deployment.test.ts asserts every destination below is
# still a real route and every source is no longer a live service slug.

/services/excavation              /services/land-clearing  301
/services/gravel-driveway-repair  /services                301
/services/drainage-solutions      /services                301
/services/shed-pad-preparation    /services                301
